{
  "about": "Kiro's calls to an MCP server over stdio, in order (D20, R6.10). The shape of the MCP TypeScript SDK's client, which Kiro uses: initialize with its client info and roots, the initialized notification, tools/list, calls carrying a progress token, a ping while a call runs, and a notifications/cancelled for a call the user stopped. A documented shape, not a recording: the GUI pass is the owner's (tasks.md §8). {workspace} is replaced by the probe.",
  "messages": [
    {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "method": "initialize", "params": {
      "protocolVersion": "2025-06-18",
      "capabilities": {"roots": {"listChanged": true}},
      "clientInfo": {"name": "Kiro", "version": "0.8.0"}}},
    {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "notifications/initialized"},
    {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "tools/list", "params": {}},
    {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "method": "tools/call", "params": {
      "name": "doctor", "arguments": {"workspace": "{workspace}"},
      "_meta": {"progressToken": "kiro-2"}}},
    {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "method": "tools/call", "params": {
      "name": "scan", "arguments": {"workspace": "{workspace}"},
      "_meta": {"progressToken": "kiro-3"}}},
    {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "method": "ping"},
    {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "notifications/cancelled",
     "params": {"requestId": 3, "reason": "The user stopped the tool."}},
    {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "method": "tools/call", "params": {
      "name": "scan_cancel", "arguments": {"workspace": "{workspace}"}}},
    {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 6, "method": "tools/call", "params": {
      "name": "scan_status", "arguments": {"workspace": "{workspace}"}}}
  ],
  "answered": [0, 1, 2, 4, 5, 6],
